research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4067-          "fact": "L3",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4068-          "source": "lem-metric-uniformity-dictionary",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4069-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.proof-contracts.json-4070-          "quote": "For a metric space $(X,d)$ with $X\\ne\\varnothing$, the sets $E_\\varepsilon=\\{(x,y):d(x,y)<\\varepsilon\\}$, $\\varepsilon>0$, generate a separated uniformity. Its induced topology is the metric topology, and uniform continuity to another metric uniformity is exactly metric uniform continuity.",
