MATHEMATICS: For nonempty \(X\), each \(E(F,\varepsilon)\) contains the diagonal; finite unions and smaller radii give directedness, and symmetry plus the triangle inequality give the uniformity axioms. The empty-carrier counterexample is excluded; the final uniform-continuity assertion follows from \(E(\{p\},\varepsilon)\).
CITATIONS: [Kunzinger, General Topology §9.4.5](https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf) directly supports the finite-intersection pseudometric-ball basis; [Wodzicki](https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf) supports the proper-filter/entourage convention.
